n system will be performed as part of the automated setup.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-30\nValid as Of: 2024-05-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2848 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Transparent Proxy for Kubernetes - Hotfix\nDescription: Transparent Proxy version 1.5.2 provides the following hotfix:    Fixed an issue that could potentially increase CPU usage for Transparent Proxy pods beyond the threshold, possibly resulting in failed requests.  Fixed an issue in the automated Istio integration which could previously prevent the Transparent Proxy from starting.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-29\nValid as Of: 2024-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2849 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Environment Association During Destination Creation\nDescription: You can now associate environments directly during destination creation. This new feature allows you to associate a destination across all environments or select specific ones from a list of available environments.  See Manage Destinations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-29\nValid as Of: 2024-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2850 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK\nDescription: Various Microsoft Teams activities are added to enhance the Microsoft 365 SDK. You can now use the Create Chat activity to create a chat with selected members, the Get Chat List activity to retrieve the list of available chats, the Send Chat Message activity to send a message in a chat, the Get Message List activity to retrieve a list of messages from a chat, the Get User Availability activity to retrieve the availability of a current user in MS Teams. See Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK - More Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-29\nValid as Of: 2024-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_ed2f3c4543df3b9c7d849be2fbf65f371f1f9d3b186ea05893aaa8b0b353d91c_v2"}